"cur":5.5,"metric":"OPM (%)","nd":1,"pct":true,"prior":5.7,"yoy":-0.2},{"cur":66,"metric":"PAT (Rs cr)","nd":0,"pct":false,"prior":63,"yoy":4.8},{"cur":2.53,"metric":"EPS (Rs, annualised, exit qtr)","nd":2,"pct":false,"prior":2.6,"yoy":-2.7}]}},"profile":{"entities":"","mgmt":"","subseg":"","themes":""},"qtr":"","ratios":[{"label":"ROE %","value":"9.2%"},{"label":"ROCE %","value":"9.9%"},{"label":"D/E","value":"0.5x"},{"label":"Int cover","value":"4.9x"},{"label":"Receivable d","value":"61.4"},{"label":"Inventory d","value":"74.2"},{"label":"Payable d","value":"121.7"},{"label":"OPM %","value":"5.5%"}],"s":"OPTIEMUS","sec":"Telecommunication","sec2":"Telecommunication","sections":{"business":[{"body":"- Claims market leadership as \"#1 in Hearables & Wearables in India - trusted by premium global brands\", within a diversified platform spanning smartphones, hearables and wearables, fintech hardware, telecom and IoT modules.\n- Describes a deliberately de-risked model: \"Exited volatile local-brand contracts, onboarded premium customers, ensuring consistent volumes\".\n- Positions the smartphone win as a deep strategic relationship rather than a contract - \"Strategic EMS partner to the brand\", with the ramp called the \"Largest single-program ramp in OEL's history\".\n- Cover glass is framed as a deep-tech moat: \"Advanced material science - capital-intensive, with high entry barriers\", executed through a 70:30 JV between Optiemus Infracom and Corning International Corp.\n- Stated vision: \"Leveraging our deep distribution expertise and world-class EMS capabilities, we aim to build a proprietary B2C product portfolio\" - identifying products where in-house manufacturing and go-to-market strengths can be fully leveraged.","src":"deck","title":"Positioning (investor deck)"},{"body":"- [JV] Cover glass is a 70:30 JV between Optiemus Infracom and Corning International Corp., branded \"BIG Tech\" in the deck.\n- [Policy] Mobile Phone Manufacturing Scheme (PLI 2.0) is a cabinet-approved Rs 62,500 crore scheme running FY27-FY31; the deck calls it a \"STRUCTURAL GAME CHANGER FOR US\" and claims first-mover advantage through the AI+ partnership and a \"FIRST-MOVER TEMPLATE\" to onboard other Indian brands.\n- [Regulation] Mandatory BIS certification for screen protectors is expected by Jan '27 and is expected to restrict grey-market imports; the deck sizes the addressable screen protector market at ~Rs 20,000 cr today (\"Market - Imports only\") with Rs 40,000 cr potential by 2030, on 60 crore smartphone users in India at ~2 pieces per year average usage.\n- [Guidance] FY27 revenue target of ~Rs 3,600 cr (~2x FY26 revenue), then 30%+ annual growth in FY28 and FY29 to a Rs 6,000 crore revenue target by FY29 - explicitly excluding any contribution from screen protectors, cover glass and the Q3 FY27 B2C launch, with drones as additional optionality.\n- [Incubation and other income] Incubation expenses for the Drones and Cover Glass businesses impacted PAT by Rs 245 Lakhs in the quarter, with core operating PAT stated at Rs 2,363 Lakhs adjusting for these; separately, Other Income of Rs 1,091 lakhs was \"primarily driven by ongoing government policy incentives (expected to be of recurring nature)\".","src":"deck","title":"Notable from the deck"}]},"sources":["investor presentation 04-08-2026","structured quarterly financials"],"thesis":"The deck positions Optiemus Infracom as an electronics manufacturing services (EMS) platform pivoting into proprietary B2C products, with growth built on \"Six Building Blocks\" - EMS scale-up led by the AI+ smartphone partnership, the MPMS/PLI 2.0 policy tailwind, screen protectors, a second B2C category, a Corning cover-glass JV and drones - targeting Rs 6,000 crore revenue by FY29.","track":{"expired_n":0,"open":[],"open_total":0,"quarters_n":0,"revisions":[],"verdicts":[],"verdicts_total":0},"val5":[{"de":0.13,"fy":"FY22","mcap":2741,"opm":3.6,"pe":null,"roe":-0.3},{"de":0.14,"fy":"FY23","mcap":1767,"